ilures)\n- (Minor) MMLU IRT results unreliable (R̂=1.08, ESS=85)\n\n**R1 Questions:** Practical value if MAE worse than raw? Separate gamma for memorized vs collateral items? Why report at N=8 when own theory says N≥30? Real-world applicability without training data access?\n\n**R1 Missing experiments:** SBC diagnostic, d100_qc_only ablation, multi-seed pooled IRT at N≥30, verbatim contamination baseline, item-level gamma heterogeneity, posterior predictive checks.\n\n**R1 Score: 3/6, High confidence**\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R1's points. Do you agree/disagree? Does anything change your score or assessment? Be specific about which R1 points strengthen or weaken the case.\n","uuid":"b1b3379f-5b82-46de-a1b5-29ba5b1e581e","session_id":"9513347c-0cdf-4b9b-9658-b8164fba2e34"}
